## Start here (session ritual)

1. Read [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md) if not already in context.
2. Check [goals/STATUS.md](goals/STATUS.md) for the current state and the log.
3. Check [work/](work/) for in-flight items and [docs/adr/](docs/adr/) for decisions
   constraining the area you're touching.
4. Compare `_commit` in `.copier-answers.yml` (the mlpipe tag this repo was rendered
   from and pins) with mlpipe's latest tag. If behind, propose `/template-sync` before
   new work.

## Where things live

- Design and boundaries → [DESIGN.md](DESIGN.md)
- Status and change log → [goals/STATUS.md](goals/STATUS.md) (the log is append-only)
- Why decisions were made → [docs/adr/](docs/adr/) (numbered, append-only; a changed
  decision is a new ADR that supersedes the old)
- Proposals and in-flight items → [work/](work/) (`NNNN-slug/`; archive, never delete)
- Pipelines → `src/{{ package_name }}/`, registered under `[project.entry-points."mlpipe.pipelines"]`
- Run data (gitignored, local): `store/`, `manifests/<pipeline>/`, `mlruns/`, `reports/`
- Repo procedures → `.claude/skills/`: `template-sync` (take a new mlpipe tag)

## Hard rules

- Steps touch the world ONLY through `RunContext` (`ctx.get`, `ctx.put`, `ctx.config`,
  `ctx.log_metric`, `ctx.log_meta`). No direct file I/O, no tracker SDK calls in steps.
- Polars DataFrames cross step boundaries; Parquet at rest. Pandas only inside a step,
  where a library requires it.
- Every step config is a `StrictConfig` (pydantic, extra keys forbidden). A new option
  goes into the schema first; never bypass validation.
- Every run goes through the CLI (`mlpipe run` / `tune` / `predict` / `promote` /
  `lineage` / `show`), never by importing internals, so every execution leaves a
  manifest.
- Step modules import what they use from submodules (`from {{ package_name }}.helpers import f`),
  not from the package root: a step's signature covers the code it imports, so a heavy
  or unrelated package root would invalidate its cache on unrelated edits.
- Promotion only via `mlpipe promote`; `baselines.yaml` is written by nothing else.
- mlpipe is a pinned library. Never patch it here: a fix goes to mlpipe, ships as a
  tag, and this repo bumps the pin (`/template-sync`).
- New dependencies need a short ADR (status: Proposed). No hosted or cloud storage of
  run data. Never commit secrets.

## When comparing experiments

Cite the fold-plan hash for both runs. If the plan hashes differ, the comparison is
invalid: say so instead of reporting a winner.

## When blocked

Environment blocks (installs, credentials, network) are human steps: stop and ask, and
record the exact ask in a `work/` item so it survives the session.

